      "content": "Do not take potassium supplements on your own, as people with stage 3 kidney disease often struggle to eliminate excess potassium, which can lead to life-threatening heart rhythms. Always consult your nephrologist or primary care provider before starting any new supplement to ensure your levels are safe. They may simply prescribe medication to manage your cramps and fatigue without risking an unsafe buildup of potassium in your system.",
