    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "okay i get that but it's just so frustrating. i was reading online that sometimes people with CKD actually get too little potassium from their diet because of all the restrictions, which makes them feel weak. if i avoid the supplements and just try to eat more potassium-rich foods like bananas or spinach to boost it naturally, is that safer? like, would that be a better way to handle it until my appointment?",
