      "content": "Even though dietary sources are generally safer than supplements, foods rich in potassium like bananas, spinach, and potatoes can still accumulate in your system due to your kidney impairment. Because potassium levels can shift quickly with diet and activity, relying solely on food without checking your levels first carries a significant risk of a sudden spike. It is strongly recommended you verify your current levels with a lab test before making any dietary changes to ensure safety.",
